OpenBSD lacks xattrs; store symlink reparse data in regular files with
Wine's '?' suffix, matching ntdll/unix/file.c. Truncate the data when
removing a reparse point so it does not become ordinary file contents.

Directory reparse points (.wine-reparse inside the directory, removed
before the directory); any reparse tag, as upstream.

